ed mass  The mass is 2 3cm from the anterior  1 2cm from the posterior  5 6cm from the medial  1 5cm from the lateral  3 5cm from the superior and 4 6cm from the inferior margins  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm defect  located between the mass and the posterior margin of resection  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm lobulated  dense fibrous area noted within the parenchyma  The remaining parenchyma consists of unremarkable tan white fibrous tissue and yellow and lobulated fat  No other discrete lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass  with the defect in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma with the dense area in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast   is a 257 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm simple mastectomy specimen  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm skin ellipse with a central nipple on the anterior aspect  There is a stitch attached to the skin which is designated 12 o clock  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregular and lobulated nodule    suspicious 9 o clock density   which is 0 4cm from the posterior margin  The remaining parenchyma consists of dense  tan white  focally cystic fibrous tissue and yellow  focally hemorrhagic and unremarkable fat  No discrete lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the suspicious nodule in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE LYMPH NODE  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2 AND 2A  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  Gross Dictation by Vincent Ko M D   on REMOVED