imen is sectioned to reveal a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm irregularly shaped tan white firm area  which abuts the inked margin  The specimen is entirely as cassettes H J  Labeled  inferior left breast margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fibrofatty tissue with a stitch designating the edge furthest from the tumor  The aspect with the stitch is inked blue and the specimen is sectioned to reveal several tan yellow nodules measuring up to 0 3cm in diameter  consistent with fat necrosis  No tumors are grossly identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes K L  Resident  Mari Mino  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 25 CLINICAL DATA  Breast lesion  right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE III III AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    COMEDO TYPE  EXAMINED INKED MARGINS ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor is 1 5cm in size and infiltrating carcinoma is present 0 2cm from the inked resection margin  Over 50  of the tumor mass centrally shows loose fibrous tissue and necrosis  No vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 26                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  negative  progesterone receptor  negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 57     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right breast  is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a poorly defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  white tan mass that extends to within 0 2cm of the margin  Tissue is frozen for estrogen receptors and the frozen section block is saved frozen  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A F   remainder of tumor with adjacent margins G I   representative surrounding tissue Resident  Daniel D  Koelliker  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Anthony Mattia  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Wiley Souba  MD PART   BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Yes.
