xtends to   0 1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within  and beyond  the region of the mass  There is an extensive in situ component present  EIC positive   GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2 MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to   0 1cm from the anterior margin of the specimen  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  NOTE  Sections of the right anterior final margin  part G  reveal a small focus of ducts distended by a proliferation of monomorphic ductal cells with a vaguely cribriform pattern  Multiple level sections through the block were reviewed  The findings in this sample are limited by the small focus of involved tissue  The differential diagnosis includes atypical ductal hyperplasia  however  the findings are morphologically similar to the areas of DCIS present in the main specimen right breast excision  part B  and are thus interpreted as a small focus of residual DCIS  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Hughes  REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan pink fatty replaced lymph node  which is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1 and FX 1A  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively  Received are 6 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast lump  short superior  long lateral   is a 5 x 4 x 1 5cm oriented tan yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating superior  long stitch designating lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned along the superior to inferior axis to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan pink  well circumscribed mass which grossly abuts the anterior margin and lies 0 9cm from medial  