Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 19 02 CLINICAL DATA  Biopsy at outside hospital showed   ductal breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  AND HEMOSIDERIN DEPOSITION CONSISTENT WITH BIOPSY SITE  FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGANCY IN 14 OF 14 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 49                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  stitch on inferior margin    is a 11 x 7 x 6cm piece of breast tissue with a 8 x 2cm skin ellipse on its surface  A 3 7cm fine suture line courses longitudinally across the skin ellipse  The medial margin has been inked black  the lateral margin red  and the deep margin green  Sectioning through the breast tissue demonstrates a central area consisting of red brown hemorrhage surrounding tan white fibrous tissue that has a stellate appearance and intervening yellow  chalky  fatty appearing tissue  The fat away from the central area has a normal yellow  glistening appearance  Grossly  there are no areas suggestive of residual carcinoma  This central area  at its closest point from the resection margin  measures 0 4cm  The central area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm in total greatest dimensions  SLIDE INDEX  A   inferior margin B C   deep margin D   superior margin E   lateral margin F through M   sections through the biopsy cavity and adjacent breast tissue  Labeled  Right axillary content  is a 9 x 6 x 2cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue and intermixed lymph nodes  The largest node measures 1 8cm in diameter and on cut section is infiltrated with fat  A representative section from each node is submitted in cassettes N through U  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  David John Mikulis  M D  PART A  PRIOR RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY SITE PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
