Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 53 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with microcalcifications on right breast mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   85    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   15    COMEDO TYPE   SEE NOTE   2  FOCAL SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 1cm in greatest diameter  Both infiltrating and in situ carcinoma are focally present at the inked resection margin  No unequivocal vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 36                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 95 at 15 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with needle localization  and accompanied by roentgenogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a variegated  firm  gritty  tan pink nodule  1 1cm in greatest dimension  located 5mm from the end of the localizing wire  and abutting the inked surface  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the breast is submitted in A through F  with the nodule predominantly in A through C  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Yes.
