ere developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 12 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast with needle localization wire  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of tan pink to yellow fibrofatty breast tissue oriented with a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture a superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  white fibrotic nodule  2 7cm from the superior margin  2 0cm from the inferior margin  1 9cm from the lateral margin  1 5cm from the medial margin  1 3cm from the anterior margin  and 1 1cm from the posterior margin  A second 0 9cm firm white nodule is  0 1cm from the anterior margin  and a 1 5cm ill defined rubbery area of fibrosis abuts the anterior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE  A D  1st mass  entirely submitted E  Smaller nodule F  Rubbery fibrosis Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast final shaved margin  superior half of cavity  are fragments of yellow adiopose tissue measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes G I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast final shaved margin  inferior half of cavity  are three irregular portions of lobulated  partially cauterized yellow adipose tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE