70  With T lineage antibodies  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of some small cells scattered within the tissue  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of a chronic lymphocytic leukemia small lymphocytic lymphoma  Special stains with congo red for amyloid is negative  A trichrome stain for collagen shows faint positivity in the eosinophilic material  A PAS stain shows occasional plasma cells positive for PAS  These stains suggest the presence of collagen but not of amyloid or macroglobulin  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  06 MAY 04 at 17 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm red  slightly firm lymph node  which is bivalved and submitted in its entirety for frozen section as FX 1  now cassette A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary node nonsentinel   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibrofatty soft tissue which is dissected for lymph nodes to reveal two tan pink rubbery lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE and 1 6cm in greatest diameter  The lymph nodes are bivalved to reveal a tan white fleshy cut surface  Specimens are submitted in their entirety as labeled  B  Larger lymph node bivalved  C  Second lymph node bivalved  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast re excision 