lts with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are four containers  Labeled  Medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm tan soft tissue fragment  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  1  and now submitted in cassette A  Labeled  Lateral margin  is a tan soft tissue fragment  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  2  and now submitted in cassette B  Labeled  Superior margin  is a tan red soft tissue fragment  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  3  and now submitted in cassette C  Labeled  Inferior margin  is a tan red soft tissue fragment  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  entirely frozen as Frozen Section  4  and now submitted in cassette D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit n