Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA  Excision of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  1   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FLORID SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH FOCAL MICROCALCIFICATIONS AND FOCAL BLUNT DUCT ADENOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE SOLID PAPILLARY CARCINOMA WITH FOCAL MUCIN PRODUCTION  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4  FLORID SCLEROSING ADENOSIS WITH FOCAL MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 20 48                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  Specimen  2  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast 