Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 17 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with extensive ductal carcinoma in situ with a focus of invasion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  CRIBRIFORM AND COMEDO TYPES  MANY MICROSCOPIC FOCI AROUND PRIOR BIOPSY SITE  ALL RESECTION MARGINS AND 17 OF 17 LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF TUMOR  2  BIOPSY SITE WITH FIBROSIS  GRANULATION TISSUE  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  HISTIOCYTIC AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION TO SUTURE MATERIAL  NOTE  No invasive carcinoma is present  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 50                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient  s name and unit number only  is a 550 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left mastectomy specimen  which includes an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm left axillary tail  and which is partially covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm skin ellipse  The specimen is oriented with sutures  The skin ellipse includes a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm areolar and a 2 0cm in length well healed transverse scar  3 0cm superolateral to the nipple  The skin is diffusely tan brown  and otherwise unremarkable  The deep resection margin is a smooth plane  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a prior REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm stellate and sclerotic biopsy site with radiating fibrous bands and focal semifirm sulphur yellow discoloration  The biopsy site is immediately subjacent to the epidermal scar  and approaches to within 0 1cm of the superior margin  1 5cm of the deep inked margin  3 0cm of the lateral margin  4 0cm of the inferior margin  and 5 0cm of the medial margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of mature  lobular  yellow  adipose tissue with interculating fibrous bands  The axillary tail is explored for lymph nodes  several lymph nodes are identified  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing one lymph node  The node is bisected and submitted in S  SECTION CODE  A C  biopsy site with superior margin and skin  D  biopsy site with superior margin  E G  biopsy site with deep inked margin  H  lateral margin  I  inferior margin  J  medial margin  K  nipple  L N  lymph nodes  low  O P  lymph nodes  middle  Q R  lymph nodes  high  S  lymph node  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Craig Scott Seidman  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY NODE  LEFT    report_end  , Checked.
