ometastasis  Clinical correlation is suggested  The entire  specimen was submitted for microscopic examination  Immunohistochemical stains  for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  keratin7  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  do not reveal evidence of carcinoma  An  atypical cell on the H E stained slide is consistent with a megakaryocyte     This case does not contain all the coding components for CMS PQRI measure  99          Electronically Signed Out By Kristina M Braaten MD       Resident Pathologist   Louis J  Vaickus MD  PhD      By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       CLINICAL HISTORY  Left breast cancer     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST EXCISION  LEFT  B  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT INFERIOR  C  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT MEDIAL  D  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT SUPERIOR  E  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT DEEP  F  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT LATERAL  G  LYMPH NODES DISSECTION  LEFT AXILLA CONTENTS    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 7 containers  which are each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     A  Received fresh  labeled  left breast needle localized lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm lumpectomy specimen which is unoriented  The specimen contains 1  guidewire and 1 unattached guidewire  The specimen is inked entirely black   The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a punctate area of hemorrhage and  presumed biopsy site  as well as multiple cysts filled with a thick  brown  fluid  ranging in size from  0 1cm to 0 4cm in maximum size  The surgical  clip is not appreciated  Additionally  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan white  to tan grey oval shaped nodule within the specimen  Representative sections are  submitted as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Aforementioned nodule    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entirety of presumed biopsy area and surrou